// ===========================================================================
// TON PRIMES — the GOVERNED TREASURY and its LP POSITION CHILDREN.
// CONCEPT.md §5.5 (§2 point 4, §3.4, §8, §9.1); DECISIONS.md D-100, as amended
// by D-147, D-167 and D-168. Contracts: contracts/contracts/primes_treasury.tolk
// and contracts/contracts/primes_lp_position.tolk. Opcodes: shared/opcodes.ts
// `TREASURY`. Parameters: shared/params.json `treasury` (governance) and
// `staking` (the distribution rate and epoch).
//
// WHAT IT IS. The team's money under holder control. The treasury holds PRIMES
// (its own genesis vest lock, D-100 point 6 / D-166), GRAM (58% of the unsold-prime
// forfeits, §4.1/§6 point 2), tsTON (D-151) and depositors' LP. It is the
// CUSTODY ADDRESS for LP that wants a vote: anyone deposits DeDust PRIMES/GRAM LP
// into one of FOUR lock terms (30 d / 3 m / 6 m / 1 y) and, while the term runs,
// that position is the electorate. LP CUSTODY EARNS NO PRIMES (D-168 deleted the
// LP miner); the treasury's PRIMES reach holders through `distribute()` to the
// stake master (stake.tlb, §5.3) instead.
//
// IT HOLDS NO PROTOCOL GRAM, and that distinction is the whole of §8. `pending`
// is the ratchet's, `owed` is the prime owners', and neither is here. Nothing in
// this family moves `T`, `S`, `pending`, `owed`, `k`, `K_CEIL` or the split, and
// NOTHING HERE MINTS (TR-4).
//
// TWO CONTRACTS, AND THE SPLIT IS A PROTOCOL LIMIT. Config 43 fixes
// `max_acc_state_cells = 65,536` per non-masterchain account, so a positions
// dictionary in one account dies around 20,000 positions: the treasury holds
// GLOBAL state and one child per wallet holds that wallet's positions.
//
// THE CHILD'S ADDRESS IS THE AUTHENTICATION. A child is deployed from the
// treasury's `position_code` with init data `(owner, treasury_addr, empty, 0, 0,
// 0, empty, 0, 0, clock_divisor)`, so its address is a hash of that code and that owner. Every
// message from a child carries `owner`; the treasury re-derives
// `positionAddress(owner)` and compares it to the sender.
//
// TWO SPEND ROUTES AND NO THIRD (TR-2): a PASSED PROPOSAL (`execute`,
// permissionless, capped at `treasury.proposal_cap_bps` of that asset's balance
// AT EXECUTE TIME) and `distribute()` (D-168 — PRIMES to the stake master only,
// at most once per interval, amount = the formula). TR-1 is DELETED with the
// miner: nothing accrues inside the treasury any more. There is no
// `update_config`, no owner field, no pause and no upgrade (D-100 point 7).
// ===========================================================================

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Treasury storage
//
// Timestamps are uint40 throughout this file — a Unix timestamp fits until the
// year 36812, and the bits bought are what let `proposal` stay in one cell.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// `distribute()`'s whole state. 267 + 32 + 40 + 124 + 32 = 495 bits.
//
// `stake_addr` and `rate_bps_per_day` are DEPLOY DATA, fixed at deploy and
// unreachable by any message. `stake_addr` is the ONE address `distribute()` can
// pay; the stake master's address does not depend on the treasury's (the master
// learns the treasury through its own one-shot `set_wallet`), so there is no
// circular dependency on this side. `rate_bps_per_day` is
// `staking.distribution_rate_bps_per_day` (19, sim-selected).
//
// `last_distribute_time` is 0 until the first `distribute()`, which is therefore
// allowed at once — the ratchet's `last_harvest_time` precedent.
distribution$_
    stake_addr:MsgAddress
    rate_bps_per_day:uint32
    last_distribute_time:uint40
    distributed_total:Coins
    distribute_events:uint32
  = Distribution;

// Balances are TRACKED, not read: a jetton balance lives on the jetton wallet and
// TVM cannot read it synchronously. `getTreasuryBalances` publishes them so a
// reader can reconcile against each wallet's own `get_wallet_data`.
// `lp_held` is Σ positions[].amount across every child — TR-5's left-hand side,
// kept here so the invariant is one get-call rather than a crawl over children.
balances$_
    primes_balance:Coins
    tston_balance:Coins                    // D-151, harvested from the ratchet
    lp_held:Coins
    primes_in:Coins
    deposit_events:uint32
  = Balances;

// One proposal. 267+8+124+267+40+40+128+128+8 = 1010 bits: deliberately inside
// the 1023-bit single-cell budget, which is what the uint40 timestamps buy.
//
// `opens` is when the VOTE opens, not when the row was written: `propose` sets
// `opens = now + notice_duration` and `closes = opens + vote_duration` (D-173 as
// amended 2026-11-19, audit R2-H1). The proposal was proposed at
// `opens − getGov().notice_duration`; no separate field stores it.
//
// `asset` is 0 GRAM / 1 PRIMES / 2 tsTON (D-151; LP is not proposable, D-167) / 3
// venue confirm (D-194: `amount` = the timelock record seq, no value moves).
// `executed` is cleared again by the bounce handler when the send failed — that
// is what makes a bounced execute retryable rather than a proposal lost forever.
proposal$_
    proposer:MsgAddress
    asset:uint8
    amount:Coins
    dest:MsgAddress
    opens:uint40
    closes:uint40
    yes:uint128
    no:uint128
    executed:uint8
  = Proposal;

// `eligible_weight` is Σ `amount · vote_multiplier` over live positions — every
// tier votes since D-168. It is the denominator of the 1% proposal threshold and
// NOTHING ELSE — there is no quorum (D-100 point 8).
//
// D-147 MADE IT AN UPPER BOUND. Nobody sends a message when a term matures, so
// terms that have ended still count here until someone sends `expire`. It is
// never wrong in the direction that lets someone in who should be out: an
// inflated denominator makes proposing HARDER.
//
// D-188 point 7: NO VOTE BOOK. Who voted is recorded on the voter's own child
// (`PositionStorage.voted`); this keeps only per-proposal totals. `proposals` is
// bounded by deletion: a row is pruned once failed and closed, or once
// `closes + vote_duration` (the execute window) has passed — by the permissionless
// `prune`, and by every `propose`, which prunes the two oldest due rows. `open_by`
// is deleted with the proposal it names.
gov$_
    proposal_seq:uint32
    eligible_weight:uint128
    proposals:(HashmapE 32 ^Proposal)
    open_by:(HashmapE 256 uint32)          // addrKey(proposer) -> their latest seq
  = Gov;

// The treasury's OWN wallets. Circular-address bootstrap (D21): a TEP-74 wallet
// is addressed by its owner. ALL THREE ARRIVE IN ONE MESSAGE; D-151's tsTON
// wallet is stored one cell over, on `TreasuryConfig`, only because a fourth
// MsgAddress overflows this cell's 1023-bit budget (3·267 + 8 = 809 already).
treasury_wallets$_
    lp_jetton_wallet:MsgAddress
    primes_jetton_wallet:MsgAddress
    wallets_set:uint8
    genesis_script_addr:MsgAddress
  = TreasuryWallets;

// `operator_addr` is D-100 point 6's operator, recorded so `getTreasuryConfig`
// can publish it — and for NOTHING ELSE. No message grants the operator any
// authority whatsoever.
//
// `clock_divisor` is D-139's test clock, dividing the vote window, the tier terms
// this contract mirrors and `distribute()`'s interval. 1 is mainnet and the
// identity. `position_code` is `primes_lp_position.tolk`, fixed at deploy.
treasury_config$_
    operator_addr:MsgAddress
    sink_addr:MsgAddress
    tston_jetton_wallet:MsgAddress
    clock_divisor:uint16
    position_code:^Cell
    w:^TreasuryWallets
  = TreasuryConfig;

// Four refs and no bits: one per kind of state.
treasury_storage$_
    dist:^Distribution
    bal:^Balances
    gov:^Gov
    cfg:^TreasuryConfig
  = TreasuryStorage;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Position-child storage
//
// THE FIELD ORDER IS PART OF THE ADDRESS, and `primes_treasury.tolk`'s
// `PositionInit` mirrors the empty state of exactly these fields in exactly this
// order. A field reordered on either side derives children nobody can reach;
// `Treasury.spec.ts` asserts the two agree.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// `tier` (0..3) is editable ONLY by `relock`, and only upward before maturity;
// the child's assert is `new_tier >= tier || now >= matures_at`.
//
// `locked_at` is WHEN THE TERM STARTED. A position matures at
// `locked_at + tier_term_seconds[tier] / clock_divisor`, and a relock restamps it.
//
// `weight_since` is SINCE WHEN THE POSITION HAS HELD ITS CURRENT VOTE WEIGHT.
// Set at deposit; a relock at the same tier before maturity keeps it, any other
// relock (an upgrade, or reviving a matured term) restamps it. `vote` carries it
// so the treasury counts only weight held before the proposal opened
// (CONCEPT §5.5.5, 1202).
//
// `in_flight` is 1 while a withdraw and 2 while a sink-forward is in flight to the
// treasury — the flag that stops the same LP being moved twice, and (D-214) the
// one that tells `confirm_withdraw` to credit `forever_amount`.
//
// `expired` is 1 once this position's vote weight has left BOTH aggregates — by
// `expire`, or because a bounced move restored it without it. NOT the vote rule
// (the rule is the clock); the flag that stops the same decrement twice.
position$_
    amount:Coins
    tier:uint8
    locked_at:uint40
    weight_since:uint40
    in_flight:uint8
    expired:uint8
  = Position;

// `vote_weight` is a running sum over the live positions, maintained on every
// credit, relock, expire and confirm — never scanned. AN UPPER BOUND between a
// term's maturity and its `expire`, exactly as `eligible_weight` is. `next_id` is
// monotonic and ids are never reused.
position_storage$_
    owner:MsgAddress
    treasury_addr:MsgAddress
    positions:(HashmapE 32 Position)
    next_id:uint32
    position_count:uint32
    vote_weight:uint120                    // Σ amount · vote_multiplier(tier), less expired
    // D-188 point 7: (seq << 32 | position_id) -> record_until = the vote's
    // `now + vote_duration`. Written before the vote is sent, refused twice
    // (1155), pruned by every `position_vote` once `now >= record_until`, deleted
    // when the vote bounces. Bounded by this owner's votes in the last window.
    voted:(HashmapE 64 uint40)
    // D-214: Σ LP this owner locked forever through `to_sink`, and when that total
    // last grew. Votes `forever_amount × 100` (`treasury.forever_vote_multiplier`)
    // under position id 0xFFFFFFFF, never matures; every credit restamps the time.
    forever_amount:Coins
    forever_since:uint40
    clock_divisor:uint16                   // D-139, inherited. LAST.
  = PositionStorage;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Inbound — treasury
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// One-shot, genesis script only, gated by `wallets_set`.
set_wallets#96000001
    query_id:uint64
    lp_jetton_wallet:MsgAddress
    primes_jetton_wallet:MsgAddress
    tston_jetton_wallet:MsgAddress
  = InternalMsgBody;

// From one of the treasury's OWN jetton wallets. Which wallet sent it decides
// what it is:
//
//   * the PRIMES wallet -> a PRIMES inflow (a vest tranche, a donation). No
//     payload is read: PRIMES here are held for a proposal or `distribute()`.
//   * the tsTON wallet -> a tsTON inflow (`harvest()`, D-151, or a donation).
//   * the LP wallet -> `forward_payload` must be `TDEP`, which credits a
//     position in the named tier and adds its vote weight to `eligible_weight`.
//
// AN ABSENT, UNRECOGNISED OR MALFORMED PAYLOAD ON THE LP WALLET, OR A TIER ABOVE
// 3, REFUNDS IN FULL to the address that sent the transfer (sink.tlb's outcome
// 2). A notification from any OTHER wallet throws (`treasury_wrong_wallet`,
// 1151). The LP arm needs `TREASURY_MIN_FORWARD` = 0.15 GRAM (103).
transfer_notification#7362d09c
    query_id:uint64
    amount:Coins
    sender:MsgAddress
    forward_payload:(Either Cell ^Cell)
  = InternalMsgBody;

// "TDEP" — a custody deposit into `tier` (0..3, `treasury.tier_term_seconds`).
// The tag is PERMANENT — it ends up in transfers already on chain.
treasury_action_deposit#54444550
    tier:uint3
  = TreasuryForwardPayload;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Inbound — treasury, from the sender's OWN child only
//
// Every one of these carries `owner`, and the treasury's only check is that
// `positionAddress(owner)` equals the sender (1152).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// D-147 / D-168. A relock restarted one position's term under `new_tier` (the
// child already refused a downgrade before maturity). The treasury moves the vote
// weight in `eligible_weight` — drops `amount · vote_multiplier(tier)` unless
// `expired`, adds `amount · vote_multiplier(new_tier)` — and nothing else. It
// pays nothing, so no reply is awaited.
relock_vote#96000002
    query_id:uint64
    owner:MsgAddress
    position_id:uint32
    amount:Coins
    tier:uint8
    new_tier:uint8
    expired:uint8
  = InternalMsgBody;

// Move a position's LP out — to the owner (`to_sink = 0`, only once the LOCK
// TERM has matured, which the child enforced) or to `primes_lp_sink.tolk`
// (`to_sink = 1`, allowed at any time, D-100 point 4). `expired` says whether an
// `expire_vote` already removed the vote weight, so the exit does not remove it
// twice. Needs 0.15 GRAM. The treasury replies with `confirm_withdraw`.
withdraw_lp#96000003
    query_id:uint64
    owner:MsgAddress
    position_id:uint32
    amount:Coins
    tier:uint8
    to_sink:uint8
    expired:uint8
  = InternalMsgBody;

// Cast ONE named position's vote weight on one proposal. The CHILD computes it —
// `amount · vote_multiplier(tier)` while the term runs, refused from the instant
// it matures — and RECORDS the vote on itself before sending (D-188 point 7);
// the treasury only tallies. Refused before `opens` (`treasury_vote_not_open`,
// 1206: the proposal is in its notice); unless `weight_since < opens`
// (`treasury_vote_locked_late`, 1202): LP locked during the notice votes NO
// (a YES needs `weight_since <= opens - notice`, also 1202, D-173 2026-11-21), LP
// locked or upgraded once the vote is open does not; and unless `closes <= record_until` (`treasury_vote_record_short`,
// 1203), so the child's record outlives the vote it guards. A refusal bounces
// and the child deletes the record.
vote#96000004
    query_id:uint64
    owner:MsgAddress
    seq:uint32
    weight:uint128
    support:uint8
    position_id:uint32
    weight_since:uint40
    record_until:uint40
  = InternalMsgBody;

// Open a proposal: transfer {GRAM | PRIMES | tsTON} to an address, or (D-194,
// asset 3) confirm a venue timelock record — `amount` = the record's `seq`,
// `dest` = the timelock, no value moves. Refused unless
// the proposer's weight is at least `treasury.propose_min_bps` of
// `eligible_weight` — a FRACTION, never a fixed token count — and unless they
// have no other proposal whose vote is still running.
propose#96000005
    query_id:uint64
    owner:MsgAddress
    weight:uint128
    asset:uint8
    amount:Coins
    dest:MsgAddress
  = InternalMsgBody;

// D-147. Forwarded by the child from the `expire` anyone may send it: take a
// matured position's vote weight out of `eligible_weight`. IT CHANGES NO RULE —
// a matured term cannot vote whether or not this has run.
expire_vote#96000007
    query_id:uint64
    owner:MsgAddress
    position_id:uint32
    amount:Coins
    tier:uint8
  = InternalMsgBody;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Inbound — treasury, PERMISSIONLESS
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Execute a passed proposal after `closes` and before `closes + vote_duration`
// (`treasury_execute_lapsed`, 1204 — D-188 point 7). Requires `yes > no` — simple
// majority of votes cast, NO QUORUM, A TIE FAILS — and `amount` at or below
// `treasury.proposal_cap_bps` of the asset's balance AT EXECUTE TIME (TR-3). For
// PRIMES and tsTON that balance is the whole tracked balance: nothing accrues
// inside the treasury since D-168. A BOUNCED EXECUTE RESETS `executed`. A venue-
// confirm proposal (asset 3, D-194) has no cap; its executor attaches
// `VENUE_CONFIRM_GAS` (0.03 GRAM), carried on to the timelock by mode 64.
execute#96000006
    query_id:uint64
    seq:uint32
  = InternalMsgBody;

// D-168 / §5.5.3 — TR-2's second exit. Sends ONE TEP-74 transfer of
//
//   budget = primes_balance · rate_bps_per_day · interval / (10000 · 86400)
//
// to `stake_addr`, with `forward_ton_amount` = 0.05 GRAM and forward payload
// `stake_action_budget#53424754` ("SBGT", stake.tlb), response_destination = the
// caller. `interval` = `staking.epoch_seconds` / clock_divisor.
//   * at most once per interval: `treasury_distribute_early` (1200) until
//     `now − last_distribute_time >= interval`;
//   * `treasury_distribute_dust` (1201) below `DISTRIBUTE_MIN_BUDGET` = one
//     nano-PRIMES — the empty treasury, and nothing else;
//   * the caller attaches `DISTRIBUTE_MIN_FORWARD` = 0.15 GRAM (103) and gets the
//     change back.
// The transfer's query_id is `(2 << 56) | previous last_distribute_time`, so a
// bounce restores `primes_balance`, the cumulative figures AND the previous
// timestamp — retryable at once.
distribute#96000008
    query_id:uint64
  = InternalMsgBody;

// D-188 point 7. Delete a proposal nothing can happen to any more: failed
// (`yes <= no`) and closed, or past `closes + vote_duration`. Also clears the
// proposer's `open_by` slot if it still names `seq`. `treasury_not_prunable`
// (1205) otherwise; `getPrunable(seq)` answers without the throw.
prune#96000009
    query_id:uint64
    seq:uint32
  = InternalMsgBody;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Outbound — treasury to the owner's child
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Credit a new position. Deploys the child if it does not exist yet. The child
// allocates the id and stamps `locked_at = now`.
lp_credit#96000010
    query_id:uint64
    amount:Coins
    tier:uint8
  = InternalMsgBody;

// 0x96000011 was `set_reward_debt`, the miner's settle reply — deleted by D-168.
// RETIRED, not recycled.

// The reply half of `withdraw_lp`: the LP has been sent, delete the position.
confirm_withdraw#96000012
    query_id:uint64
    position_id:uint32
  = InternalMsgBody;

// BOUNCE RECOVERY ONLY. The LP transfer bounced, so the position
// `confirm_withdraw` deleted is put back — MATURED (`locked_at = 1`, 1970, so
// every term is already served) and `expired`, since its vote weight left
// `eligible_weight` before the LP was sent and is not restored. The owner is
// recovered from the failed transfer's `response_addr`, deliberately the OWNER on
// both the withdrawal and the sink-forward. `from_sink` (D-214) is bit 40 of the
// failed transfer's `query_id`: 1 takes back the forever credit the confirm made.
restore_position#96000013
    query_id:uint64
    position_id:uint32
    amount:Coins
    tier:uint8
    from_sink:uint8
  = InternalMsgBody;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Inbound — the position child, from the OWNER only (except `expire`)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// 0x96000020 (`request_withdraw`, D-147) and 0x96000022 (`claim`, the miner's
// payout, D-168) are RETIRED, not recycled.
//
// withdraw / to_sink / relock need POSITION_MIN_FORWARD = 0.20 GRAM (103), the
// owner (1164), a held id (1165) and no move in flight (1168).

// Take the LP back. ONE MESSAGE, refused until `matures_at`
// (`position_term_running`, 1166).
withdraw#96000021
    query_id:uint64
    position_id:uint32
  = InternalMsgBody;

// Forward one position's LP to the LP sink — locked depth, forever. NO MATURITY
// GATE (D-100 point 4).
to_sink#96000023
    query_id:uint64
    position_id:uint32
  = InternalMsgBody;

// Cast ONE named position's vote; forwarded to the treasury as `vote`. A matured
// term is refused (`position_no_vote_weight`, 1169), and a second vote from the
// same position on the same proposal (`treasury_already_voted`, 1155 — the
// child's own record, D-188 point 7).
position_vote#96000024
    query_id:uint64
    seq:uint32
    support:uint8
    position_id:uint32
  = InternalMsgBody;

// Open a proposal on ONE named position's weight; forwarded as `propose`.
position_propose#96000025
    query_id:uint64
    asset:uint8
    amount:Coins
    dest:MsgAddress
    position_id:uint32
  = InternalMsgBody;

// D-147. Restart the term at `now` under `tier` (0..3; 102 above). Refused as a
// DOWNGRADE while the current term still runs (`position_relock_downgrade`,
// 1167). Applied on the child, then forwarded as `relock_vote`.
relock#96000026
    query_id:uint64
    position_id:uint32
    tier:uint8
  = InternalMsgBody;

// D-147, and THE ONE MESSAGE ON EITHER CONTRACT WITH NO SENDER CHECK. Mark a
// matured position's vote weight gone, here and — via `expire_vote` — in the
// treasury's `eligible_weight`. Moves no asset, changes no rule, IDEMPOTENT (an
// already-expired position returns). Needs 0.20 GRAM.
expire#96000027
    query_id:uint64
    position_id:uint32
  = InternalMsgBody;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Outbound — assets
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// GRAM, on `execute` of an asset-0 proposal. It carries a body so the bounce
// handler gets the proposal sequence back to reset `executed`.
ton_payout#96000014
    query_id:uint64
    seq:uint32
  = InternalMsgBody;

// D-194, on `execute` of a passed venue-confirm proposal (asset 3): to `dest`, the
// venue timelock, which sets `confirmed` on the record whose `seq` this names. No
// value beyond the executor's hop. A refusal (stale seq, a vote that opened
// before the record was queued, or one that closed before the record's `eta` —
// audit H1) bounces and resets `executed`, like a GRAM payout.
confirm_venue#a0000006
    query_id:uint64
    seq:uint32
    vote_opens:uint40   // the proposal's `opens`
    vote_closes:uint40  // the proposal's `closes`; the timelock needs >= its `eta`
  = InternalMsgBody;

// Every asset the treasury can move — PRIMES on a proposal or `distribute()`, LP
// on a withdrawal or a sink-forward, tsTON on a proposal — moves as a plain TEP-74
// transfer from the treasury's own wallet. LP NEVER moves as a DeDust withdraw.
//
// `query_id` is packed `(tag << 56) | …` so `onBouncedMessage` can tell which
// arm bounced from the body alone — tag 1 execute (| asset << 32 | seq), 2 distribute (| the
// previous last_distribute_time), 3 an LP position move (| tier << 32 | position
// id), 4 a deposit refund.
//
// `response_addr` is the OWNER on every position move (see `restore_position`),
// the caller on `distribute()`, and the treasury itself on `execute` (hence its
// `excesses#d53276db` arm).
transfer#0f8a7ea5
    query_id:uint64
    amount:Coins
    destination:MsgAddress
    response_addr:MsgAddress
    custom_payload:(Maybe ^Cell)
    forward_ton_amount:Coins
    forward_payload:(Maybe ^Cell)          // "SBGT" on distribute(), else none
  = InternalMsgBody;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Get-methods (§9.1 — every number a surface shows maps to one of these)
//
// -- the treasury --
//   getDistribution()         -> (last_distribute_time, interval, rate_bps,
//                                 next_budget_estimate, distributed_total,
//                                 stake_addr)
//                                `interval` is clock-divided; the next
//                                `distribute()` is due at last + interval.
//                                `next_budget_estimate` is the handler's own
//                                formula over today's balance.
//   getTreasuryBalances()     -> (ton_balance, primes_balance, lp_held,
//                                 primes_in, tston_balance)
//   getGov()                  -> (proposal_seq, eligible_weight,
//                                 proposal_cap_bps, propose_min_bps,
//                                 vote_duration, notice_duration)
//                                both durations clock-divided; a proposal's
//                                vote opens `notice_duration` after `propose`
//   getProposal(seq)          -> (proposer, asset, amount, dest, opens, closes,
//                                 yes, no, executed)
//   getExecutable(seq)        -> (executable, reason, cap, available)
//                                `reason` is the error code the call WOULD
//                                throw, or 0. Exact for every asset.
//   getVotable(seq)           -> (votable, reason) — would the block clock accept
//                                a `vote` now; reason 1153 / 1206 (notice) / 1154
//   getPrunable(seq)          -> 0 | 1 — would `prune(seq)` succeed now
//   getTreasuryCounts()       -> (deposit_events, distribute_events)
//   getVoteMultipliers()      -> the four VOTE multipliers (1, 3, 10, 30)
//   getTierTerms()            -> the four LOCK TERMS, seconds, clock-divided
//   getPositionAddress(owner) -> that owner's child, deployed or not
//   getTreasuryActions()      -> TDEP
//   getTreasuryMinForward()   -> (treasury_min_forward, distribute_min_forward)
//   getTreasuryConfig()       -> (lp_jetton_wallet, primes_jetton_wallet,
//                                 operator_addr, sink_addr, wallets_set,
//                                 tston_jetton_wallet)
//
// -- the position child --
//   getPositions()            -> (position_count, next_id, vote_weight)
//   getPosition(id)           -> (amount, tier, locked_at, expired, in_flight,
//                                 matures_at). `matures_at` is the instant
//                                 `withdraw` stops throwing AND `vote` starts
//                                 throwing.
//   getVoteWeight()           -> this wallet's vote weight, less what `expire`
//                                has retired. AN UPPER BOUND between a maturity
//                                and its `expire`; the RULE is never approximate.
//   getTierTerms()            -> the four LOCK TERMS as the CHILD enforces them
//   getPositionOwner()        -> (owner, treasury_addr)
//   getPositionMinForward()   -> nominal GRAM an owner message must forward
//   getHasVoted(seq, id)      -> 0 | 1: this position holds a vote record on
//                                `seq` (D-188 point 7; forgotten once the
//                                proposal has certainly closed)
//   getVotedCount(seq)        -> how many of this wallet's positions hold one
//
// THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO `getSolvency` ON EITHER CONTRACT. §3.4 reconciles GRAM
// balances against declared GRAM LIABILITIES; the treasury owes its GRAM to nobody
// and the child holds no assets at all. The PRIMES liability this family used to
// carry (TR-1, the miner's accrual) moved to the stake master as ST-1 (D-168).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
